Hi,

  I am using XFS on  MD RAID-5  array. I am  testing the RAID-5
stability by pulling one drive and then I run filesystem consistency
check to see if there is any corruption. There is data loss after I run
the xfs_repair commands. My question is, does barrier would help in
maintaining the file system integrity in this scenario ? I know barrier
is more use-full in the event of power failure. What about the disk
failure ? Probably MD should be able to take care of this right. But
with XFS I am seeing issue. Whereas ext-3 seems to fine.

=20

Regards,

Marri


